# Decision log discipline

- Before implementing a material architectural or financial-domain decision,
  check `docs/decisions/` for an existing ADR.
- If none exists, run `scripts/adr.sh "<short title>"`, complete the ADR, and
  include it in the same change as its implementation.
- Log assumptions when the brief or a provider is ambiguous. If Corgi later
  answers differently, add a superseding ADR; never erase the earlier decision.
- Add cuts to `docs/decisions/CUT_LIST.md` when they are made, not at freeze.
- Mention the ADR in the eventual commit message: `[ADR-NNNN]`.
- Do not log implementation trivia. Log decisions a reviewer can reasonably ask
  “why?” about: dimensions, accounting, time semantics, algorithms, thresholds,
  provider behavior, security boundaries, and scope cuts.
